This project depends on the following third-party software. None of it is
vendored/bundled in this repository — it is installed separately via pip
(see requirements in the venv) and, for Piper, invoked as an external tool.

Permissive dependencies (MIT / BSD / Apache-2.0):
  - numpy            BSD-3-Clause (+ bundled 0BSD/MIT/Zlib/CC0 components)
  - onnxruntime       MIT
  - pathvalidate      MIT
  - flatbuffers       Apache-2.0
  - protobuf          BSD-3-Clause
  - packaging         Apache-2.0 OR BSD-2-Clause
  - Piper voice model "en_US-amy-medium" (rhasspy/piper-voices)   MIT

Weak-copyleft dependency:
  - pygame-ce         LGPL v2.1
    Used as an ordinary imported library, unmodified. LGPL v2.1 explicitly
    permits linking/importing from software under any license without
    imposing its terms on that software, provided the library itself is
    not modified.

Strong-copyleft dependency (used as an external tool only):
  - piper-tts (the `piper` CLI)   GPL-3.0-or-later
    This project does NOT import piper-tts as a Python library. It is
    invoked as a separate subprocess (see SpeechEngine in game.py), with
    text piped in and a WAV file read back out. Running an independent
    GPL-licensed executable as a subprocess is aggregation, not linking,
    and does not extend GPL terms to this project's own code.
